From: nexumia-de <https://github.com/nexumia-de>
Subject: wolfssljni: guard the session store against concurrent use

WolfSSLAuthStore keeps the cached sessions in a LinkedHashMap that
connections on several threads read and change at once. Setting the
session timeout walks it while another connection adds a session, which
throws ConcurrentModificationException. F-Droid sets the timeout in its
hostname verifier for every connection and crashed while downloading
with several connections.

Upstream wolfssljni does every access to the store under storeLock;
this is the minimal backport for the vendored copy.

Upstream: https://github.com/wolfSSL/wolfssljni/blob/master/src/java/com/wolfssl/provider/jsse/WolfSSLAuthStore.java
